    Weak: every view of one value keeps it the same way, narrowed Weaks stay handles, and the finder sees generic instantiations
    
    Reviewer R's findings on integrate-5 and integrate-6 (review/integrate5/weak on claude/task-k9saws),
    each now a fixture and a mutant caught by it alone:
    
    1. tsc lets { v: Box } and { v: Weak<Box> } be seen as each other, and (x: Weak<Box>) => ... as
       (x: Box) => ..., so one slot was read as a handle through one type and a target through the other
       (a_objview3 printed false where Node prints true; the rest segfaulted). Only arrays and maps were
       checked. Now every value flowing into a place with a type of its own (an initializer, an
       assignment, an argument, a return, a spread, an as) is compared position by position: every field
       the view has, every element, key and value, every parameter and result, all the way down, Weak in
       both or in neither, or it's NotYet. Five probes; the mutant that skips the comparison is caught by
       exactly those five.
    2. filter and every, through the predicate the checker infers for x => x !== undefined, leave an
       array of Box & WeakBrand, which lowered as plain objects while the elements were still handles
       (a_filter2 printed 1 -1 false, a_every false, a_filter segfaulted). An element or map value
       narrowed from a Weak is kept as a Weak now, and so is a for...of variable over one.
       weak_narrowed.a; the mutant keeping it as its plain representation is caught by it alone.
    3. Cycles through generic classes passed the finder and leaked: Box<Node> made only as Box<T> inside
       Maker<Node>, and a captured let of type T instantiated with a function. Lowering now gives each
       instantiation its concrete types (its class type, its this, its locals and function values, and
       again for every instantiation sharing a lowered instance), through the checker's own
       instantiateType, pulled by linkname as the shim does for what it exports (instantiate.go; it
       belongs in cohere's shim). Two probes; the mutant without instantiation is caught by those two.
    4. A narrowed Weak<Map> crashed the compiler reading type arguments off Map & WeakBrand. They're read
       through the brand now, as are a narrowed Weak array's. weak_narrowed.a holds it; the mutant
       reading them off the brand crashes the compiler on that fixture alone.
    5. The mutant remove_entry writing EMPTY instead of TOMBSTONE survived. weak_test.go now runs
       reviewer R's a_probechain.a and a_reuse.a, each side held to its own output, and probe_chain.a
       catches it (UBSan, a store through a stale handle).
    
